{"kind":"request","text":"Rule on two concrete choices for hosted cards 288d5988, following builder question 3b0d7d52.\n\nThe implementation in builder/hosted-cards-20261102 shares McpService.fromInstalledApplication between node.ts:serve and HostedAgent. On first startup it makes one complete bounded native query of active installations, with limit 2. Exactly one active declared installation selects cards after exact siblings, package IDs, definition, trusted publisher and immutable bytes match. Missing, incomplete or multiple rows select no card tools. Each card read rechecks the installation. Stdio reads the immutable public Git package; the Worker reads its trusted APPLICATION_CONTENT. The service keeps this selection for its process or object lifetime; restarting selects again. Explicit declaredViews callers keep their own selection. Please accept this scope or name the selection and refresh behavior you require.\n\nFor a host without UI capability, tools/list keeps model opening tools as text, strips their _meta.ui and omits app-only view_read/view_act. This is the existing stdio behavior. Existing stdio resources/list and resources/read still serve HTML resources to an authenticated caller that requests them explicitly; UI capability has never been authority. Please say whether this slice must also hide HTML resources or strip their UI metadata from non-UI resource replies.\n\nThe new native route witness passes: hosted and stdio card lists/bytes agree, both remote origins appear, non-UI tool metadata is absent, ambiguous selection loads nothing, Counter's controller-only act refuses the agent, and a separate fixture action records the hosted agent's own key. Bearer rotation during held source setup also passes. Deployed hosted MCP remains closed; no live host setup has run.","body":{"conditions":"The planner rules on sole-active-installation selection and restart behavior, and on resource replies for a host without the UI capability.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}